bt_editor
=========

Behaviour Tree visual editor built on Dear PyGui.

Features
--------
* Node-based editor: connect Composites, Decorators, and Behaviour nodes via
  drag-and-drop links
* Built-in node library:
    * Composites: Sequence, Selector, Parallel
    * Decorators: Inverter, ForceSuccess/Failure, Repeat, RetryUntilSuccess,
      Timeout, SuccessIsRunning
    * Behaviours: auto-discovered plugins (P2P, SimpleAction, VisualServo, …)
    * Utilities: Value, Vector, Math, VectorTransform, Blackboard
    * Robotics: HTMatrix, RPY<->HTM, PoseCompose/Inverse/Error, JointState,
      ScalarToVector, VectorSplit, Gain, Dot/CrossProduct
    * Vision: BlobDetector, ContourAnalysis, ColorMask, CornerDetector,
      TemplateMatch, LineDetector, Centroid
    * Input: Image source node
* Blackboard editor: define and inspect shared key-value entries at runtime
* YAML save / load (preserves node positions, links, and blackboard)
* JSON export for use with external BT executors
* Context menu, clipboard (copy/paste sub-trees), demo graph loader
* Debug overlay with real-time node-status highlighting

Requirements
------------
* Python >= 3.13
* dearpygui >= 2.2
* opencv-python >= 4.13
* py-trees >= 2.4
* pyyaml >= 6.0
* psutil >= 7.2
* rich >= 15.0

Usage
-----
    uv run main.py

or, with the virtualenv activated:

    python main.py

